aisdk 1.5.0 

a data frame's rows
  sent     : print(d[2:3, ])
  received : print(d[2:3])
  CHANGED (jsonlite alone gives the text back unchanged: TRUE)

an empty column index
  sent     : m <- x[order(x$a), ]
  received : m <- x[order(x$a)]
  CHANGED (jsonlite alone gives the text back unchanged: TRUE)

a trailing comma before a brace, as in text or JSON inside a string
  sent     : the set {a, b, } is written so
  received : the set {a, b} is written so
  CHANGED (jsonlite alone gives the text back unchanged: TRUE)

a single-quoted name before a colon
  sent     : x <- c('a': 1)
  received : x <- c('a': 1)
  unchanged

a name after a comma, before a colon
  sent     : f(x, y: z)
  received : f(x, y: z)
  unchanged

plain text
  sent     : which row does the circle draw?
  received : which row does the circle draw?
  unchanged

an element id
  sent     : e28
  received : e28
  unchanged

4 of 7 valid arguments reach the tool unchanged

the step that changes them (aisdk:::repair_json_string), on the first:
  {"code":"print(d[2:3])"} 
